WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:19.564
Henry and his friends said good-bye to Nathan and Nora, and then hurried down the street toward the Martins' house.

2
00:00:19.565 --> 00:00:24.290
On the way Henry explained how he'd realized that Marty was the thief.

3
00:00:24.291 --> 00:00:27.572
"It's the only possibility," he said.

4
00:00:27.573 --> 00:00:31.383
"We already proved that none of our other suspects did it.

5
00:00:31.384 --> 00:00:34.601
Besides it makes perfect sense."

6
00:00:34.602 --> 00:00:37.322
"It does?" Cole said.

7
00:00:37.323 --> 00:00:39.525
"Sure," Henry said.

8
00:00:39.526 --> 00:00:43.640
"Everyone else at the lemonade stand was distracted, remember?

9
00:00:43.641 --> 00:00:46.764
Those two teenage girls were giggling together."

10
00:00:46.765 --> 00:00:52.701
Maggie grinned. "They were probably planning their shopping trip to the drugstore!"

11
00:00:52.702 --> 00:00:55.744
"Probably," Henry agreed.

12
00:00:55.745 --> 00:01:00.707
"And Ryan was busy chugging his lemonade and doing tricks with his skateboard."

13
00:01:00.708 --> 00:01:04.910
"And I was talking to Nathan and Nora," Maggie remembered.

14
00:01:04.911 --> 00:01:10.127
"Even Mrs. Martin was distracted by her cell phone," Henry said.

15
00:01:10.128 --> 00:01:15.160
"While nobody was paying attention, Marty must have grabbed the cash."

16
00:01:15.161 --> 00:01:17.598
"And then what?" Cole asked.

17
00:01:17.599 --> 00:01:21.611
"Like Maggie said, there was too much money to hide in Nora's hands.

18
00:01:21.612 --> 00:01:24.074
And Marty's hands are even smaller."

19
00:01:24.075 --> 00:01:27.355
"He didn't need his hands," Henry said.

20
00:01:27.356 --> 00:01:31.016
"He stuffed it in that toy suitcase he was holding."

21
00:01:31.017 --> 00:01:37.404
Maggie gasped. "Henry, you're a genius!" she shrieked.

22
00:01:37.405 --> 00:01:42.186
"It's the perfect hiding place! Why didn't I think of that?"

23
00:01:42.187 --> 00:01:46.190
"There was no reason to remember it," Henry pointed out.

24
00:01:46.191 --> 00:01:48.983
"Little kids always have toys, right?"

25
00:01:48.984 --> 00:01:51.956
"So how come you remembered?" Cole asked.

26
00:01:51.957 --> 00:01:55.316
"I didn't at first," Henry admitted.

27
00:01:55.317 --> 00:02:00.377
"But when Nora was talking about Marty, I started thinking about him.

28
00:02:00.378 --> 00:02:05.128
That's when I remembered the suitcase and realized what must have happened."

29
00:02:05.129 --> 00:02:08.044
They had almost reached the Martins' house.

30
00:02:08.045 --> 00:02:11.890
Henry could see Mrs. Martin out in the yard with Marty.

31
00:02:11.891 --> 00:02:13.810
She saw them coming.

32
00:02:13.811 --> 00:02:18.703
"We were just about to go back to your house, Maggie!" she called out.

33
00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:22.899
"I discovered something very interesting in Marty's suitcase."

34
00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:28.793
"You did?" Maggie hurried over. Henry and Cole were right behind her.

35
00:02:28.794 --> 00:02:32.415
Marty's suitcase was lying open in the front yard.

36
00:02:32.416 --> 00:02:34.587
Cash was spilling out of it!

37
00:02:34.588 --> 00:02:38.372
"My money!" Maggie cried happily.

38
00:02:38.373 --> 00:02:42.429
"So Marty was the thief," Cole exclaimed.

39
00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:47.995
Mrs. Martin smiled. "I just discovered Marty playing with all this cash.

40
00:02:47.996 --> 00:02:54.995
At first I couldn't imagine where it came from, but then I figured out what must have happened," she said.

41
00:02:54.996 --> 00:03:00.071
"Sorry, Maggie. Marty likes to grab everything these days.

42
00:03:00.072 --> 00:03:03.749
He must have grabbed your money while I wasn't looking."

43
00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:07.765
"We just figured that out ourselves," Henry said.

44
00:03:07.766 --> 00:03:10.156
"Yeah," Cole chimed in.

45
00:03:10.157 --> 00:03:13.132
"Henry put together all the clues and solved the mystery."

46
00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:16.620
"You did?" Mrs. Martin looked impressed.

47
00:03:16.621 --> 00:03:21.569
"Good work, Henry. Maybe you'll be a police detective when you grow up."

48
00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:27.211
"It wasn't just me," Henry said. "These guys helped."

49
00:03:27.212 --> 00:03:31.249
Cole grinned. "Yeah, solving mysteries is fun.

50
00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:36.275
It's sort of like solving the puzzles on the Puzzle Pirates website, only better."

51
00:03:36.276 --> 00:03:41.766
Mrs. Martin smiled back. "Well, keep up the good work," she said.

52
00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:47.945
"Now I'd better get Marty inside and explain to him why we don't steal other people's things.

53
00:03:47.946 --> 00:03:52.869
It would be awfully embarrassing to have to arrest my own son!"

54
00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:57.537
"Don't worry, Mrs. Martin." Maggie started gathering up her money.

55
00:03:57.538 --> 00:03:59.680
"I won't press charges."

56
00:03:59.681 --> 00:04:04.702
Mrs. Martin chuckled. Then she picked up Marty and went into the house.

57
00:04:04.703 --> 00:04:09.233
Maggie kept scooping up her money. Cole watched her.

58
00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:13.324
"Aren't you going to share some of that with us?" he asked with a grin.

59
00:04:13.325 --> 00:04:20.219
Maggie looked up. "Share my money?" she said. "Why would I do that?"

60
00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:25.871
"Usually when people solve a mystery, they get a reward," Cole pointed out.

61
00:04:25.872 --> 00:04:28.848
Maggie didn't say anything for a second.

62
00:04:28.849 --> 00:04:31.694
She had a thoughtful look on her face.

63
00:04:31.695 --> 00:04:34.705
"What's the matter?" Henry asked her.

64
00:04:34.706 --> 00:04:38.141
"Are you trying to figure out how much our reward should be?"

65
00:04:38.142 --> 00:04:43.163
"No," Maggie said. "But I am thinking about rewards.

66
00:04:43.164 --> 00:04:47.708
What if we turned the lemonade stand into a detective agency?

67
00:04:47.709 --> 00:04:51.691
That might be a faster way to earn money for my riding lessons!"

68
00:04:51.692 --> 00:04:57.311
Cole laughed. "The Lemonade Detectives?" he joked.

69
00:04:57.312 --> 00:05:03.309
"Why not?" Maggie smiled. "We did a great job solving this mystery.

70
00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:07.840
We could solve other mysteries for people, and they could pay me."

71
00:05:07.841 --> 00:05:11.067
"Pay you?" Henry said.

72
00:05:11.068 --> 00:05:15.354
"Okay, okay. Pay us," Maggie said.

73
00:05:15.355 --> 00:05:18.932
"You guys could each get 10 percent of our rewards."

74
00:05:18.933 --> 00:05:21.387
Henry and Cole traded a look.

75
00:05:21.388 --> 00:05:25.063
Without a word they turned and started to walk away.

76
00:05:25.064 --> 00:05:31.108
"Wait!" Maggie ran after them. "I meant to say 15 percent."

77
00:05:31.109 --> 00:05:33.849
Henry and Cole kept walking.

78
00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:40.791
"Fine!" Maggie sounded annoyed. "We can split the money evenly."

79
00:05:40.792 --> 00:05:45.056
"That's more like it." Henry stopped and turned around.

80
00:05:45.057 --> 00:05:46.539
So did Cole.

81
00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:52.335
"If you throw in all the free lemonade we can drink, you have yourself a deal," he agreed.

82
00:05:52.336 --> 00:05:56.943
"Okay." Maggie nodded. "So let's have a cheer.

83
00:05:56.944 --> 00:06:00.514
Hooray for The Lemonade Detectives!"

84
00:06:00.515 --> 00:06:02.461
"Hooray!"

85
00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:07.439
Henry grinned. He liked the sound of The Lemonade Detectives.

86
00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:16.471
"Now all we need is another case!"
